const CORE_HARNESS = "*** THIS IS A CORE PIPELINE. THE HARNESS IS JEST AGAINST A REAL POSTGRES. ***\n\nThe last pipeline was `apps/web` under vitest in jsdom with no database at all. This one is\n`apps/core`, and AGENT-RULES rules 19 and 20 were written for exactly this harness. They apply in\nfull. Do not carry vitest habits into it.\n\n  RUNNING THE SUITE (on the server, always):\n      pnpm --filter @hmis/core test                                             # the whole suite\n      pnpm --filter @hmis/core exec jest --passWithNoTests <path>                # one file\n      pnpm --filter @hmis/core exec jest --passWithNoTests <path> -t \"<name>\"    # one test, ISOLATED\n\n  RULE 19 IS NOT ADVICE, IT IS A TRAP THAT HAS ALREADY FIRED.\n  `pnpm --filter @hmis/core test -- <path> --testNamePattern=X` DOES NOT ISOLATE: pnpm injects a\n  literal `--`, yargs stops option parsing, and your pattern becomes a second test-PATH pattern.\n  The WHOLE suite runs and you get a false \"the single test passed N times\". Bypass the script with\n  `exec jest` as above, and prove isolation FROM THE OUTPUT - the \"N skipped, 1 passed\" line -\n  never from an exit code.\n\n  RULE 20 IS LIVE IN THIS PIPELINE. The per-worker database name derives from JEST_WORKER_ID,\n  which is per-process and COLLIDES ACROSS AGENTS: another agent's truncate breaks your run\n  mid-measurement and looks exactly like a real flake. Before you trust ANY timing, race, flake or\n  concurrency measurement, run `pgrep -af jest` and READ THE MATCHED COMMAND LINES. (Careful: a\n  `pgrep -af jest` inside a command whose own text contains the string \"jest\" matches ITSELF -\n  read the lines, do not count them.) Say in your report whether you observed interference.\n\n  MIGRATIONS ARE IRREVERSIBLE HOST MUTATIONS - AGENT-RULES section 6. Running `db:generate` and\n  letting a suite migrate it MUTATES ALL PER-WORKER DATABASES, and `git checkout` does not undo\n  it. The one time this was got wrong it left fourteen orphan tables and a phantom migration row\n  in seven databases, turned origin/main itself RED on the host with no commit containing the\n  cause, and cost ~934k tokens for zero delivered tasks. **ONLY T1 GENERATES A MIGRATION.** If you\n  are not T1 you run `pnpm db:generate` NEVER, for any reason, not even to check something.\n\n  `pnpm verify` is the ROOT command (typecheck + lint + every workspace's tests) and it is what you\n  end on - DETACHED, with the exit VALUE read from a file, never held open on a foreground SSH\n  channel, which exits 255 on a dropped link and destroys the evidence mid-run.\n\n  NEVER run bare `tsc` or `tsc -b` (rule 5). Jest resolves `.js` before `.ts`, so stale emit\n  silently shadows your sources and the failure looks like anything but what it is."

