const BASELINE = "BASELINE - MEASURED, WITH ITS TIMESTAMP, AND IT HAS A SHELF LIFE\n\nMeasured by the MAIN SESSION on the build host, 2026-08-21 at commit `5aff6ac`, full detached\n`pnpm verify` (typecheck + lint + every workspace's tests), exit VALUE **0** READ FROM A FILE,\nwith nothing else running under jest:\n\n    apps/core           119 suites / 763 tests\n    apps/web             30 files  / 144 tests\n    packages/contracts    3 suites /   7 tests\n\nYour own baseline is THE PREVIOUS TASK'S COMMIT - whatever `git rev-parse origin/main` returns when\nyou start. This pipeline is strictly sequential and docs commits land from the owner's machine\nwhile it runs (rule 11), so origin/main WILL have moved. That is not drift, it needs no\ninvestigation, and it needs no reconciliation paragraph. Pull and work.\n\n*** RE-CONFIRM BEFORE YOU TRUST IT (EXECUTION-LESSONS 2.21). *** A measured baseline has a shelf\nlife inside a pipeline that mutates shared state - and this one's FIRST TASK APPLIES A MIGRATION\nto every per-worker database, which is precisely the mutation 2.20 is about. Before you start, run\none cheap shipped suite and confirm the host is still green:\n\n    pnpm --filter @hmis/core exec jest --passWithNoTests src/kernel/crypto.test.ts\n\nIf it is NOT green, that is a FINDING to report, not your bug and not something to work around.\nSay so and stop.\n\nCOUNTS - AGENT-RULES section 4. **There is NO per-task test-count target in this plan and none in\nthis brief.** The rule is: the workspace total must NOT DECREASE, your diff must DELETE NO TEST,\nand you quote the runner's own summary line for the suites you added, BY EXACT PATH. If a number\ndisagrees with what you measure, REPORT the difference and its cause. Never pad, split, merge or\ndelete a test to hit a number."

